    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leading the charge at a 72.87 efficiency score. Despite the difficulty of facing Chris Bassitt, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from an advantageous batting order position and high xwOBA metrics that anchor his projection. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a top-tier play at 70.59; although he faces a platoon disadvantage against Patrick Corbin, the elite park factors and his cemented role in the #2 hole elevate his floor significantly. **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and **Miguel Vargas** (63.37) round out our core; **Miguel Vargas** is particularly interesting today as he avoids the platoon penalty that hampers other lefties in our lineup, positioning him for a high-volume production day against Rojas.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Jung**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a solid 61.01 score. While **Josh Jung** projects well against the weak xERA of Spencer Arrighetti, the optimizer favored the structural consistency of **Miguel Vargas** and the park-adjusted ceiling of **Coby Mayo**. We are monitoring the rain risk for **Dominic Smith**; at a marginal 43.22, he is the most volatile asset in our lineup today. Given that **Dominic Smith** is facing a 35% rain risk against Payton Tolle, we are prepared to pivot if the weather forecast deteriorates further, as his score is currently too thin to withstand a rain-shortened outing.",
